      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Patients with ileal endocrine tumors have a good survival rate."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To assess the quality of life of patients with endocrine tumors of the ileum."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS",
          "content": "Forty-four consecutive patients (30 males, 14 females, mean age 61.1 years, range 26-79) with proven endocrine tumor of the ileum were studied."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Italian version of the SF-12 Health Survey (SF-12) questionnaire able to explore the physical and mental aspects of daily life were used. Forty-four sex-matched and age-matched Italian normative participants were also considered for SF-12 evaluation."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The overall analysis of the SF-12 questionnaire in the 44 patients showed values of physical component summary (PCS) and mental component summary (MCS) scores representative of a relatively good quality of life and not significantly different from those of the normative population (PCS: 46.5+/-10.3 vs. 47.0+/-4.7, P = 0.792; MCS: 45.9+/-10.8 vs. 49.1+/-2.0, P = 0.057). PCS was significantly impaired in nonsmokers (P = 0.028), in those who underwent less invasive surgery (P = 0.007), in those who had pain at onset of the disease (P = 0.002), and in those who received multimodality treatment (P = 0.013). To evaluate the factors independently related to PCS, a multivariate analysis was performed and we found that specific surgery (P = 0.046) and presence of pain at onset of the disease (P = 0.001) were the only two factors that showed an independent relationship with PCS."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The patients with endocrine tumor of the ileum seem to perceive their quality of life as relatively good."
        }
      ]},
